# Training samples for the "spell this word" intent.
# {word} is an open slot filled with whatever the user asks to have spelled.
# Alternations (a|b) and optionals [x] keep the phrasings consolidated instead
# of one line per wording, see OVOS-INTENT-1 §3.
# "letter by letter" and "for me" are trailing politeness/manner phrases: they
# are listed as optionals so they are not swallowed into {word}.
(how do you|how to|how would i) spell [(out|word|the word)] {word} [letter by letter] [for me]
(can|could|would) you spell [(out|word|the word)] {word} [letter by letter] [for me]
spell [(out|word|the word)] {word} [letter by letter] [for me]
how (is|are) {word} spelled [letter by letter]
[can you] (what is|what's|what) the spelling of {word}
[(can|could|would) you] (tell me|give me) the spelling of {word}
[the] spelling of [the word] {word}
{word} how do you spell (that|it)
